
  carino-pbx — Asterisk + FreePBX telephony appliance

  Web UI      http://<this host>/          (first visit creates the admin account)
  Setup log   journalctl -u freepbx-setup  (FreePBX installs itself on first boot)
  Control     fwconsole start|stop|restart|reload
              Asterisk is managed by FreePBX, not by systemctl — asterisk.service
              is masked on purpose.
  Update OS   bootc upgrade && systemctl reboot
  Update PBX  fwconsole ma upgradeall && fwconsole reload

Data lives in /var and /etc. On bootc the image's /var is copied in once at
install and is never refreshed by `bootc upgrade`, so nothing below is in the
image and nothing below is restored by an image rollback:

  /var/lib/mysql        FreePBX databases   <- crown-jewel backup
  /etc/asterisk         generated dialplan  <- crown-jewel backup
  /var/www/html         the FreePBX web tree
  /var/lib/asterisk     sounds, AGI, firmware
  /var/spool/asterisk   voicemail and recordings

